// Work over several frames: a `@job fn` runs its body one part a frame, up to each `yield`
// (language.md §16.3). `f.start(...)` takes its owned parameters and makes a `Job<f>`;
// `job.resume(...)` takes its `borrow` and `mut` parameters, runs it to its next `yield` or its
// end, and says which (`Step`).

use std::hash::StateHash
use std::serialize::Serialize

/// A job of the `@job fn` `F` (`Job<realize>`, from `realize.start(...)`): where it stopped, and
/// the locals it needs after that point. An owned value with no projections in it, so a field
/// of the program's state can hold it. Its parts are where it stopped and each local it holds:
/// it's `Clone`, `StateHash` and `Serialize` when they are, derived from them as a struct's are
/// from its fields (§16.3's job values), so a simulation's state can hold one.
pub struct Job<F>: StateHash + Serialize {}

/// What a job's `resume` did: it stopped at a `yield` (its work for this frame), or it ran to
/// its end, and gave its result.
pub enum Step<R> {
    Yielded,
    Done(R),
}
